# Line-ending normalization.
#
# This repository is developed on Windows but built and tested on Linux in CI,
# so Git stores every text file as LF and checks it out as LF everywhere.
# Without this, the same file flips between CRLF and LF depending on which
# machine committed it, producing diffs that are pure noise and masking the
# real change underneath.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the one consumer that genuinely needs CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never apply text handling to these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
